{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 4a0b3454700a97e09a44099ec6d6af610d795740 (tree da5ab6632ae0f8f6aeee4d79deb0c686d60a8632), the BO1-W1 notes-only plan for hosting the Commons witness on dap-commons, on published c9038871. The verdict binds the BO1-W1 implementation promise and signs the one path artifact, notes/implementation/2026-11-22-bo1-w1-commons-plan.md (63be010f). It approves the plan as a note. It authorizes no provisioning, deploy or register change, which stay with the planner and Hugh.\n\n## What the head is\nThree notes-only commits on c9038871 change one file (`git diff --name-only c9038871 4a0b3454`): the plan (da69aa9f), its gate evidence (d827e5b2) and the sequencing of the register pin review (4a0b3454). No source, test or config file changes.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Gate.** The notes-only gate ran on da69aa9f (tree 2f9fec1f). `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `c8cd67ee…`) names that head and tree, shows \"changed files 0\", and ends \"gate passed\" in 35.92 s. `git diff --name-only da69aa9f 4a0b3454` lists only the plan, so the notes-only rule covers the head.\n- **Hash.** The one SHA-256 in the note matches `gate.txt` in the retained directory.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (c9038871) is clean with tree da5ab663. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 3. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines hold no credential, token, private key, private CLI home path, other project's name or `/Users/` path. The note names `SESSION_SECRET` by key only.\n\n## Claims I checked against source at c9038871\n- **Expiry order.** `planInstall` signs with `lifetimeSeconds: PROPOSED_BOUNDS.intentLifetimeSeconds - 60`, and `intentLifetimeSeconds` is 15 × 60, so the plan lives 14 minutes. `registerIdOf(signed, definition)` derives the register ID from the signed intent, which carries `notAfter` and a nonce, so a refreshed plan gives a different ID. The note's order is right: the register ID cannot be known before the plan, the timed config commit changes only the two register values, and a refresh needs a new ID. `executePlannedInstall` refuses `plan-expired` before any send and keeps the original home, and its comment says an exact attempted replay may recover an accepted genesis after expiry while the server refuses a never-accepted expired creation. The note says the same.\n- **The three config keys.** `apps/room/wrangler.commons.jsonc` holds `REGISTER_SCOPE: \"unplanned\"`, `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope: \"unplanned\"` and `DEMO_START_CONFIG` with `register: \"unplanned\"`. `demoCreationConfig` requires `register` to be a two-key scope reference, so the string fails it, and `fetch.ts` passes `env.DEMO_START_CONFIG !== undefined` to the page route, so the presence of the key shows the Page Start link. The note's reason for removing it is correct. `demo-config.test.ts` currently asserts the unplanned value, so step 1 must change that test, as the note says.\n- **Gates that read the config.** `demo-config.test.ts`, `security-settings.test.mjs` and `security-entry-points.mjs` read `wrangler.commons.jsonc`, the three the note names. `security-settings.test.mjs` checks the name, entry and kind of the Worker, not the register values. The route inventory runs in `npm run pins`.\n- **CLI.** `--cohort commons` is in `CREATION_INSTALL_COHORTS`, `--register-policy keys` is a valid `RegisterPolicy`, and `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` in the config lists register@23, directory@22, membership@9, rules@14, destination@16, inbox@1 and commons@1, as the note says, so Register 23 is in the creation policy.\n- **Witness bounds.** `examples/commons-bill/witness.ts` admits at most 128 requests and aborts at 120 s per invocation, as the note says. The request table sums correctly: 25 preflights at 16 scoped requests each give 400, 299 receipt-and-text pairs give 598, 23 acts and 25 or 26 final reads give 1,046 or 1,047. The 19 agent notes plus Hugh's four marks make the 23.\n- **Custody.** The note keeps the founder key with Hugh, the CLI home owner-only and private, secrets by key, and no automatic destructive cleanup. An attempted send is reconciled, never replaced.\n\n## Not checked from source\nI did not trace the index adapter's classification of `create` under `SCOPE_INDEX_MODE=enforce`. The note presents it as supported bootstrap and asks for verification after deploy. The existing local BO1 witness and the deployed creation check carry it.\n\n## Wake rate\nThe plan adds a new Worker, not a change to a published one. It adds no alarm, retry or reschedule in code. The note states a code-based floor of zero periodic archive wakes for an idle, confirmed scope and says the total Worker rate is unmeasured. The note's guard is sound: five-minute windows during W1 with a stop above 500 requests, and an idle hour after W1 that blocks further use above 100. The cost of one room, 23 notes, is about 1,046 scoped requests in an hour, and the DO fanout is unmeasured. No existing Worker changes, so the published wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged.\n\n## Architecture\nThe plan separates a structural review (remove `DEMO_START_CONFIG`, relax the test) from the timed two-value change, and defers the focused-validation exception to a planner ruling before it runs. That keeps the 14-minute window from forcing a skipped gate.\n\n## Security\nThe plan creates no open creation setting, keeps `SCOPE_INDEX_MODE=enforce`, uses keys-only founding, keeps founder custody with Hugh and reads the register identity from one retained plan. The note's reasoning about `DEMO_START_CONFIG` removes a Start link that would advertise an unusable offer.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Read an idle baseline before Hugh's block.** The note reads the idle hour after W1. A Worker whose idle rate exceeds 100 an hour would then block further use after Hugh's 40 to 60 minutes. Deploy, found the register and read a 10 to 15 minute idle window first, so Hugh's block starts on a Worker already known to idle low. dap-grow idles at about 29 requests a minute with several rooms, so the code-based zero is worth measuring early.\n2. **Archive coverage reads zero.** None of the seven cohort pins (register@23, directory@22, membership@9, rules@14, destination@16, inbox@1, commons@1) appears in `ARCHIVE_NATIVE_DATA` in `packages/git/src/archive-policy.ts`. The note prices archive wakes for \"other archive-bound\" scopes. If none of this cohort is archive-eligible, that estimate is an upper bound. Say so in the note, and the idle reading will confirm it.\n3. **Open points stay open.** The \"Decisions and missing evidence\" section keeps W1 content, agent role, operator and the focused-gate exception for the planner. This approval does not close them.\n\n## Planner act e53e0500\nI read the planner's advance ruling on the timed path (e53e0500). It approves the two-step order and authorizes the focused path for step 2 only: `demo-config.test.ts`, `security-entry-points.test.mjs`, `security-settings.test.mjs` and `npm run pins`, with the commit changing only `REGISTER_SCOPE` and `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope`. That matches the note's plan and my source checks above. The ruling sets an 8-minute approval stop and a 10-minute deploy stop inside the 14-minute plan. It asks for a checker standby window. This verdict is a review of the note and does not schedule that window. If the planner sends the timed review as a request to the checker, I can cover the diff against the retained ID and the four logs, and the planner should say when the plan starts. A peer act grants nothing beyond what my role already does, and this one asks only for a review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:63be010fc6f07b43bfeee6d13af540d9257ada82","binding":"assigned","head":"4a0b3454700a97e09a44099ec6d6af610d795740","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e53e0500b151c42049e65b30310042dedcdd46ae\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ef1283b79237cc3fd5972d6e9fc2fd3e94273ea\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5087f259abaa7f7a1834e0fe74d5957e85d49a08\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2374253a778b17059f43d91f84cddcfd5c3de60","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}